        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(sessions): reject non-canonical raw transcript cursors",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where raw transcript pagination accepted non-canonical variants of OpenClaw-issued continuation cursors. Appended junk, base64url padding, and extra JSON fields could all resume from the same SQLite transcript position as the canonical cursor.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nRaw transcript cursors now require both their base64url bytes and their complete decoded envelope to round-trip exactly to OpenClaw's encoder output. This follows the existing Plugin SDK contract: `SessionTranscriptRawDeltaLimits.cursor` is documented as an opaque cursor returned by a prior page, and `docs/plugins/sdk-runtime.md` tells callers to pass the opaque `page.cursor` into the next call. The only bundled runtime caller does not rewrite cursors, and the same canonical round-trip rule is already used by the ACP, OpenCode, and Pi opaque cursor parsers. Pagination queries, cursor fields, reset reasons, and the SQLite schema are unchanged.\n\nThe compatibility risk is bounded to undocumented cursor rewriting. No public `v*` release tag contains the commit that introduced `readSessionTranscriptRawDelta()`; `v2026.7.2-beta.3`, the newest published release when checked, predates it.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMalformed or structurally altered raw transcript cursors now return the existing `invalid_cursor` reset instead of silently continuing from an equivalent position. Canonical cursors emitted by OpenClaw continue to page normally.\n\n## Evidence\n\nOn Node v24.18.0, I drove the real `readSessionTranscriptRawDelta()` SDK runtime against a real temporary SQLite transcript store. The same harness inserted transcript events, read the first page, then supplied its canonical cursor and three altered variants. `OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR` was isolated to a temporary proof directory.\n\nBefore, using the unmodified `upstream/main` production file, every cursor variant continued as a page:\n\n```text\nBEFORE canonical: page\nBEFORE appendedJunk: page\nBEFORE padding: page\nBEFORE extraField: page\n```\n\nAfter the fix, canonical continuation still works while all non-canonical variants take the existing reset path:\n\n```text\nAFTER canonical: page\nAFTER appendedJunk: reset invalid_cursor\nAFTER padding: reset invalid_cursor\nAFTER extraField: reset invalid_cursor\n```\n\nContract and release checks:\n\n```text\ndocs/plugins/sdk-runtime.md: Pass the opaque page.cursor into the next call.\nsrc/config/sessions/session-accessor.types.ts: Opaque cursor returned by a prior page or reset result.\ngit tag --contains 3bac9093d84 --list \"v*\"\n# no output\ngit merge-base --is-ancestor 3bac9093d84 v2026.7.2-beta.3\n# exit 1: beta.3 predates the raw cursor API\n```\n\nFocused and targeted checks after merging current `upstream/main`:\n\n```text\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/plugin-sdk/session-transcript-runtime.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests       20 passed (20)\n\n./node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check src/config/sessions/session-accessor.sqlite-delta.ts src/plugin-sdk/session-transcript-runtime.test.ts\nAll matched files use the correct format.\n\n./node_modules/.bin/oxlint src/config/sessions/session-accessor.sqlite-delta.ts src/plugin-sdk/session-transcript-runtime.test.ts\n# exit 0\n\ngit diff --check\n# exit 0\n```\n\nThe repository lint wrapper could not reach its lint phase because the existing linked-worktree dependency install reports unrelated `packages/net-policy/src/ip.ts` type errors after the latest main merge; the target files pass direct `oxlint`, and the fresh fork CI run covers the full repository gates. No live agent turn was run; the affected behavior is fully exercised through the production SDK runtime and SQLite store without substituting the cursor parser or database path.\n\nAI-assisted: Codex helped implement and review the change; the production-path proof and focused test were run manually.",
